                %a{:href => "#indexed_semisimplicial_sets"} Indexed semi-simplicial sets
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#in_dependent_type_theory"} In dependent type theory
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em semi-simplicial set
            is like a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{X_n\}_{n \in \mathbb{N}}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            together with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            called
            %em face maps
            between them which encode that an element in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n+1}
            has
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            “faces” (boundary segments) which are elements in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n}
          %p
            The semi-simplicial set version of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complex"} simplicial complex
            is also called a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Delta+set"} Delta set
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            denote the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleton"} skeleton
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totally+ordered+sets"} totally ordered sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_+
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wide+subcategory"} wide subcategory
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            containing only the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+functions"} injective functions
            (it is sometimes written
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi inj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{inj}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_i
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{\Delta}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta'
            or
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\Delta}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_+
            is equivalent to the category of inhabited finite totally ordered sets and order-preserving injections.
          %p
            Recall that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\colon \Delta^{op}\to Set
            %strong semi-simplicial set
            is a presheaf
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo +
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\colon \Delta_+^{op} \to Set
          %p
            More generally, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            any other category, a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo +
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_+^{op} \to \mathcal{C}
            is a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-simplicial+object"} semi-simplicial object
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#AdjunctionWithSimplicialSets Adjunction with simplicial sets
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimplicialSets"} SimplicialSets
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of semi-simplicial sets is given by precomposition with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+functor"} opposite functor
            of the non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wide+subcategory"} wide subcategory
            inclusion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi inj
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi j
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Delta_{inj} \xrightarrow{\;j\;} \Delta
          %p
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            and hence has both a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            as well as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            given by left/right
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
