          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
            of the left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+pair"} adjoint pair
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi j
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mo !
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \xrightarrow{ \;\eta_X\; } j^\ast j_! X
          %p
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            in the sense that its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            is so (
            %a{:href => "#RourkeSanderson71"}> Rourke &amp; Sanderson 71, Rem. 5.8
            ).
          %p Notice that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimplicialSets"} SimplicialSets
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
                of the underlying semi-simplicial set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi j
                        %mo *
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^\ast X
                is the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fat+geometric+realization"} fat geometric realization
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                (see
                = succeed "):" do
                  %a{:href => "geometric+realization+of+simplicial+topological+spaces#FatGeometricRealization"} there
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo ‖
                        %mi X
                        %mo ‖
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mo |
                        %msup
                          %mi j
                          %mo *
                        %mi X
                        %mo |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\left\Vert X \right\Vert
                      \\;\coloneqq\;
                      \\left\vert j^\ast X \right \vert
            %li
              %p
                There is (by
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/source/geometric+realization+of+simplicial+topological+spaces#FatRealizationOfGoodSimplicialSpaces"} this Prop.
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
                from the fat to the ordinay geometric realization of a simplicial set (which is always “
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+simplicial+topological+space"}> good
                ” when regarded as a simplicial space):
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo |
                        %msup
                          %mi j
                          %mo *
                        %mi X
                        %mo |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi whe
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mo |
                        %mi X
                        %mo |
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\left\vert j^\ast X \right \vert
                      \\;\simeq_{whe}\;
                      \\left\vert X \right \vert
                      \\,.
          %p
            It follows (see also
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/75101/381"} MO:a/75101
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+counit"} adjunction counit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi j
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  j_! j^\ast X \xrightarrow{\; \epsilon_X \;} X
          %p
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+weak+equivalence"} simplicial weak equivalence
          %h3#relation_to_semicategories Relation to semi-categories
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semicategory"} semicategory
            is a semi-simplicial set (satisfying the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+conditions"} Segal conditions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
          %h3#model_category_structure Model category structure
          %p
            There is a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+semi-simplicial+sets"} model structure on semi-simplicial sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred
            along the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            from the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
          %h3#the_lattice_of_subtoposes The lattice of subtoposes
          %p
            Since the maps in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_+
            are all strictly monotone, any object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
            receives only (finitely many) morphisms from objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [m]
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\leq n
            whence all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slices
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_+/[n]
            are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+category"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topologies
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_+
            to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rigid+topology"} rigid
            whence all subtoposes of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo +
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\Delta_+^{op}}
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+of+a+topos"} essential
            and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf type
            and their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice"} lattice
            is isomorphic to the lattice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy-complete+category"} Cauchy-complete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategories
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_+
          %p
            This situation is familiar from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            but in the latter case there are fewer Cauchy-complete subcategories available, since an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
            having non-trivial idempotents its inclusion automatically requires the presence of all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [m]
            with
            = succeed "<" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,n
            in the subcategory whence there are countably many subtoposes corresponding to the
            = succeed "-truncated" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0],\dots ,[n]
            (plus the two trivial subcategories).
          %p
            Recall that an
            %span.newWikiWord
              essential localization
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/essential+localization"} ?
            of a topos embeds the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subtopos"} subtopos
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            (i.e. sheaves for the corresponding topology) as well as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            we call the presheaves in the image of the latter inclusion
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
                \-skeleta
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aufhebung"} Aufhebung
            of such a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+of+a+topos"} level topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            is defined as the largest topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{j}
            such that all
            = succeed "-skeleta" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            = succeed "-sheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{j}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{j}
            exists). This differs somewhat from the definition given at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aufhebung"} Aufhebung
            but will suffice in the present context where all subtoposes are
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+of+a+topos"} levels
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topologies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo +
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\Delta_+^{op}}
            are indexed by infinite words
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            over the alphabet
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                  %mo ≤
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w\leq j_z
            iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi i
                  %mo ≤
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_i\leq z_i
            for all letter positions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i=0,1,2,\dots
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 000
                  %mi …
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 000\dots
            (resp.
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 111
                    %mi …
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 111\dots
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{0}
            (resp.
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{1}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mn 0
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0^m
            (resp.
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 1
                      %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1^m
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m=0
            denotes a block of length 0 of that letter (=its absence in that position) e.g.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mn 1
                    %mi m
                  %mover
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1^m\bar{0}\;, m=0,1,\dots
            denotes all words that start with a possibly empty finite block of 1s followed by an infinite sequence of 0s (and sometimes by abuse also
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{1}
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo =
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m=\infty
            i.e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mn 1
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1^\infty
            preempts the occurrence of the second infinite block).
          %p
            The information contained in the
            = succeed "-th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            is whether the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure+operator"} closure operator
            corresponding to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
            adds
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_i=1
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_i=0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mover
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{\bar{1}}
            adds all semi-simplices of every dimension implying that the empty subobject is
            = succeed "-dense" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mover
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_\bar{1}
            = succeed "-sheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mover
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_\bar{1}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mrow
                      %mn 111
                      %mi …
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi max
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{111\dots}=j_max
            while
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mover
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_\bar{0}
            where no semi-simplex of any dimension is added and every presheaf is a
            = succeed "-sheaf" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mover
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_\bar{0}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mi min
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_min
            = succeed "-th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            is as specifying whether
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [i]
            is (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_i=0
            ) or is not (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_1=1
            ) contained in the image of the subcategory inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi j
                        %mi w
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{j_w}\hookrightarrow\Delta_+
            corresponding to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
          %p
            A topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
            restricts to a topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w|_n
            on the n-truncation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_+|_n
            by taking the prefix of length
            = succeed "+1" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mn 00
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mn 01
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mn 10
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mn 11
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{00},j_{01},j_{10},j_{11}
            are the four topologies on the 1-truncation, the topos of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver"} directed graphs
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo +
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\in Set^{\Delta_+^{op}}
            is a
            = succeed "-sheaf" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
            precisely when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_0=0
            since otherwise every
            = succeed "-sheaf" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mi w
                      %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{0w'}
            correspond to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subtopos"} dense subtoposes
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo +
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\Delta_+^{op}}
            \.
          %p
            There is a countably infinite number of co-atoms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            contains exactly one 0. These correspond to different copies of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            induced by the inclusion of the one-morphism category on the objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_+
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+negation"} double negation
            copy
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{\neg\neg}
            corresponds to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mover
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{0\bar{1}}
            = succeed "-sheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo ¬
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{\neg\neg}
            = succeed "-semi-simplexes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            = succeed "-semi-simplex" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-1-semi-simplices" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-semi-simplex." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-skeletal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mi max
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{max}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mi max
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo ¬
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{j}_{max}=j_{\neg\neg}
          %p
            We denote the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+topos"} quasi-closed
            topologies by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q(k)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            indicates the position where the 0 occurs e.g.
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo ¬
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q(0)=j_{\neg\neg}\,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [k]
            corresponds to the non-trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoidal
            subcategories of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_+
            the subtoposes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi j
                        %mi k
                        %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo +
                        %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{j^0_k}(Set^{\Delta_+^{op}})
            are the only non-trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+topos"} Boolean
            subtoposes of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo +
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\Delta_+^{op}}
            = succeed "-skeletal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi j
                      %mi k
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^0_k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo +
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\Delta_+^{op}}
            is given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\mapsto \coprod_{X[k]}[k]
            (in particular, the
            = succeed "-skeleta" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q(k)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\simeq \coprod_{X[k]}[k]
            ). This basically replaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by its “set” of
            = succeed "-semi-simplices" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-semi-simplex" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [k]
            is
            = succeed "-skeletal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q(k)
            = succeed "-precise" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-semi-simplex" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-semi-simplices)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-1
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi k
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0\leq n\leq k+1
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k\neq 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi o
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{q}(k)=o(k+1)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi o
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 0
                        %mi m
                      %mover
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o(m):= j_{0^m\bar{1}}
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subtopos"} open topologies
            to be described below.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topologies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial sets
            can similarly described by infinite words over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1\}
            with the same interpretation of the letters but there
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            has to start with a (possibly empty, possibly infinite) block of zeros expressing that the respective sheaf categories consist of
            = succeed "-truncated" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m+1
            is the length of the block of zeros with which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            starts e.g.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mrow
                      %mn 00
                      %mover
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{00\bar{1}}
            corresponds to the 1-truncation, the topos of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+graph"} reflexive graphs
          %p
            In
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo +
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\Delta_+^{op}}
            these topologies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mn 0
                    %mi m
                  %mover
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi m
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w=0^m\bar{1},\quad m=0,\dots ,\infty
            correspond precisely to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subtopos"} open subtoposes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            1 of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mo +
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\Delta_+^{op}}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
            where the degeneracies prevent this, we can truncate 1 at arbitrary dimensions by simply discarding the higher dimensional semi-simplices. Hence there is a countably infinite number of non-trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subterminal+object"} subterminal objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_n
            around this time with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_n([k])=\empty\, ,\, k\geq n+1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subtopos"} open subtopos
            is equivalent to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo +
                        %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\Delta_+^{op}}/U_n
            but clearly this is equivalent to the full subcategory of semi-simplicial sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X([k])=\empty\, ,\, k\geq n+1
          %p
            These are precisely the
            = succeed "-skeleta" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi o
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o(m)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi o
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o(m)
            defined above whereas the
            = succeed "-sheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi o
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o(m)
            = succeed "-semi-simplices" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\geq m
            = succeed "-skeletal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi o
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o(m)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is an
            = succeed "-sheaf" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi o
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi m
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o(m+1)
            = succeed "-sheaf" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_{m+1}=1
            since
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi m
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X[m+1]=\empty\,
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi o
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi o
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi m
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{o}(m)=o(m+1)\,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aufhebung"} Aufhebung
            of
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \empty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi max
                  %mo =
                  %mi o
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{max}=o(0)
            passes stepwise
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi o
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi o
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o(m)\to o(m+1)
            exactly through the open subtoposes except the “subtopos at
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi o
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi min
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o(\infty)=j_min
            for which
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi o
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi o
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{o}(\infty)=o(\infty)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 0
                        %mi m
                      %mover
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 0
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi m
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{j}_{0^m\bar{1}}=j_{0^{2m-1}\bar{1}}
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\geq 2
            (cf.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aufhebung"} Aufhebung
            for more on this case).
          %p
            Before determining the topologies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c(m)
            for the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subtopos"} closed subtoposes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join"} join
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                  %mo ∨
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w\vee j_z
            of two topologies is given by the topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{w\vee z}
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo ∨
                  %mi z
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (w\vee z)_i=w_i
            in case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_i=z_i
            or else
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi z
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (w\vee z)_i=1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                  %mo ∨
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w\vee j_z
            is given by the intersection of the two sheaf toposes. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meet"} meet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w\wedge j_z
            is given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{w\wedge z}
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi z
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (w\wedge z)_i=w_i
            in case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_i=z_i
            or else
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi w
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi z
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (w\wedge z)_i=0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
            of a topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
            is given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mover
                      %mi w
                      %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{\overline{w}}
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi w
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi i
                  %mo ≠
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{w}_i\neq w_i
            for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            e.g. for an open topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi o
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 0
                        %mi m
                      %mover
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} o(m) =j_{0^m\bar{1}}
            the closed complement
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi o
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c(m)=\neg o(m)
            is given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 1
                          %mi m
                        %mover
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{1^m\bar{0}}
          %p
            The open and closed topologies are far from being the only complemented topologies - the letter flipping operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo →
                  %mover
                    %mi w
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w\to\overline{w}
            provides a
            %em complement
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mover
                      %mi w
                      %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_\overline{w}
            for
            %em every
            topology
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
            but a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebra"} Boolean algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi ℕ
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_\mathbb{N}\mathbf{2}
          %p
            Let us call a topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
            %em locally closed
            when the corresponding sheaf topos is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+closed+subtopos"} locally closed
            i. e.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_w
            is the join of an open and a closed topology. The locally closed topologies that are neither open nor closed themselves are then necessarily of the form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 1
                          %mi n
                        %msup
                          %mn 0
                          %mi m
                        %mover
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{1^n0^m\bar{1}}
          %p
            For further details on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere-Tierney+topology"} Lawvere-Tierney topologies
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure+operator"} closure operators
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaves
            involved in both cases see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#RHE24"} Rosset-Hansen-Endrullis (2024)
          %h2#History Historical and terminological remarks
          %p
            The original paper
            %a{:href => "#EilenbergZilber50"} Eilenberg &amp; Zilber 50
            defined both (what we now call) semi-simplicial sets, under the name
            = succeed "," do
              %em semi-simplicial complexes
            = succeed "." do
              %em complete semi-simplicial complexes
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+complex"} simplicial complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
            is uniquely determined by its vertices. Then they added the degeneracies and a corresponding adjective “complete.”
          %p
            Over time it became clear that “complete semi-simplicial complexes” were much more important and useful than the non-complete ones. This seems to have led first to the omission of the adjective “complete,” and then the omission of the prefix “semi” (and at some point the replacement of “complex” by “set”), resulting in the current name
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
          %p
            The concept is essentially the same as that of
            = succeed "-set," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#RourkeSanderson71"} Rourke &amp; Sanderson 71
          %p
            On the other hand, in other contexts the prefix “semi-” is used to denote absence of identities (such as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroup"} semigroup
            (which is, admittedly, missing more than identities relative to a group) or a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semicategory"} semicategory
          %p
            Note also the existence of an alternative terminology “presimplicial sets”, or “pre-simplicial sets”, which can be traced back at least to the textbook “Cellular Structures in Topology” by Fritsch and Piccinini in 1990. This terminology is commonly used e.g. in the context of simplicial models for concurrent programs or higher-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automata"} automata
            (see e.g. “First introduction to simplicial sets” by
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sina+Hazratpour"} Sina Hazratpour
          %p
            Similarly, the subcategory of injective functions of the simplex category was written
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            at some time of the history (e.g. in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#RourkeSanderson71"} Rourke &amp; Sanderson 71
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_+
            emphasizes that it is the subcategory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            that raise the degree when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            is seen as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+category"} Reedy category
            but the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +
            may also ambiguously suggests that it adds something to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi inj
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{inj}
            emphasizes that it is the subcategory of injective morphisms of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_i
            though less explicitly. The notation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{\Delta}
            (e.g. in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Friedman12"} Friedman
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta'
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\Delta}
            (e.g. in
            = succeed ")" do
